WEBVTT

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:15.880
You see, the photos for the graduation album were
presented by the cameraman who accompanied us.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:20.250
Apparently, Yanase-sensei, who is in charge,
found this when checking through them...

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.630
She says that it appears to be...
the student, Natsuo Fujii.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.290
Do you dispute that?

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.130
Does the fact that you are staying silent,
mean that this is the truth?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.170
Regarding this... How much has been made public?

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:45.630
Right now, Yanase-sensei and I know. After this,
we will confirm the facts with Natsuo Fujii as well-

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.130
Tachibana-sensei...

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.960
Please don't do something like that.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.210
I understand. I've done something unforgivable.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.540
I don't care what happens to me.
I will accept any kind of punishment.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.420
However...

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.290
I'm begging you. In regards to this... Please! Please...!

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.510
Please

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.960
Well, time flies.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.460
There are only ten days left this year, too.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:27.920
Each of us should look back at our respective year and...

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.630
Aw... It's chilly again today.
Each of us should look back at our respective year and...

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.630
But when I think that winter break starts tomorrow,
I feel like I'm on top of the world!
We should think about "how we've grown," as a new year begins.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.580
But when I think that winter break starts tomorrow,
I feel like I'm on top of the world!
Let's aim to challenge ourselves and continue on steadily.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.000
Every day will be a festival.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:40.290
Now then, there is a teacher who will
be transferring at the end of this trimester.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:44.080
As soon as break starts, it'll be Christmas right away,
huh? I'll buy a cake and go to Hina's place...
I'd like to have this person make an address at this time.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.210
As soon as break starts, it'll be Christmas right away,
huh? I'll buy a cake and go to Hina's place...
What?!

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.670
No way! Hina-chan...?

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.750
I apologize for taking up time in this way
during the closing ceremony.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:07.790
As the Principal just mentioned, at this time,
due to personal reasons, I will be transferring schools.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.290
As this is rather sudden, for the students...

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.250
especially to all the 2nd-years whom I've been teaching,
I am sorry that this announcement is late.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.080
A substitute teacher will be taking over
starting in the 3rd-trimester.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.460
What?! No! No way!
A substitute teacher will be taking over
starting in the 3rd-trimester.

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.580
She didn't say anything about it, right?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.920
Is she getting married? Some kinda scandal?
Sensei, don't quit! Please stay until we graduate!

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.080
Thank you.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:24.790
Why?!

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:29.170
This school is the first place that I was posted at
as a teacher, and it is a very memorable place.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.630
I believe that I may have been
an inexperienced teacher to you all,

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:39.250
but I feel that I was allowed to mature along with you,
so I am full of gratitude.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:44.290
I will use what I have learned here as encouragement
to do my best at my new post as well.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.750
Thank you for all of the memories.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:49.710
I will never forget about any of you.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:56.920
Natsuo...!

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.080
Had you heard anything about Sensei?

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.580
Nothing... You? At all?

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.580
No... I hadn't really been able to see her
because of tests and stuff recently.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.330
But I was exchanging texts and phone calls...
And she was cheerful like normal, so...

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.460
Calling

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.500
We're gonna go ahead and head home, okay?

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.040
O-okay...

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.460
See ya next year!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.390
Call in progress

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:24.000
The number you have dialed is out of the coverage area-

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.830
FACULTY ROOM

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.540
Um, is Tachibana-sensei...?

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.130
You should go home for the day.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:35.960
But...

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.290
Uh... All right...

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.080
Kiriya-sensei...

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.460
Thank you for helping me out as well, Kiriya-sensei.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:55.960
Please watch over my younger sister
in the Literature Club-

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.290
Were you found out? By the higher-ups.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:07.790
You see, I had some suspicions about certain things.
After reading the novel that Fujii-kun wrote.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:16.040
I don't intend to censure you. It's just that
I was thinking how unfortunate fate can be.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.420
What?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:21.130
This was around the time
that Hagiwara-kun was your teacher.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.670
Shuu-san...?

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:28.170
At the time, he also had
special feelings for you, his student...

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:33.880
After all, there is a part of the feeling of
falling in love with someone that can't be helped,

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:35.960
regardless of age difference or social standing...

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.500
I... didn't know that...

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:45.210
If I'd consulted you, Kiriya-sensei, just like Shuu-san had,
then maybe it wouldn't have come to this...

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.330
No... it's no use...

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.670
I think that no matter how much
you might have opposed it,

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.130
I probably wouldn't have been able
to hold back this feeling.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:21.960
Hina...

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.330
Why...?

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:25.500
Why...?!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.930
To: Natsuo-kun

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.170
The fact that this letter will be the last,
is something that I ask for you to please forgive me for.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.330
I'm sure you're probably confused
at the suddenness of things.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.880
In regards to the transfer at this time, I requested it.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:54.750
The reason is because our relationship
was found out by the school.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:06:00.040
Even though you said that you wanted me to talk to you
about anything, I'm sorry for having kept silent.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:06.290
But if you had found out about this, you probably
would've thrown everything away and chosen me.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.920
I just couldn't tell you.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:14.920
In exchange for my leaving,
our relationship will not be made public.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:20.000
So, you absolutely cannot tell anyone about this.
Also, please don't come looking for me.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.630
What I wish for, is for you to move on
from me as soon as possible,

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.540
and to achieve your dream of becoming a novelist.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:28.960
That's all.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:34.710
The truth is, I should've talked to you
before this all happened.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.670
I'm sorry. I'm a weak person.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.580
I got to be with you for three months.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:47.630
The things that made us close and the things
that made us worry were all the happiest of times.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:48.630
Thank you.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:53.670
Even as I write this, the words that you said to me,

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:58.250
and the scent of your hair, and your warm hands,
and your smile are all things that I can't stop recalling.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:01.130
I'm sorry.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:02.960
I love you.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:05.630
I love you...

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.380
Café

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.380
L'AMANT

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.790
You can't find out where your older sister went?

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:20.960
No. Apparently, she called
my mom's cell phone just once, but...

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.460
So that Natsuo-chan wouldn't go chasing after her, huh?
So, how's Natsuo-chan?

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.540
He didn't come home that day.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:32.000
When I searched for him,
he was in Hina-nee's empty apartment.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.920
It's been one week since then, but...

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.830
he's still holed up in his room doing nothing.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:42.580
Honestly, I don't know what to say to him...

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.000
Hey, Natsuo!

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.000
I hear that you've gone into liquid state again?

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.790
Huh, looks like you're just about to vaporize.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:01.790
I've known about this from when your love
was still unrequited, so I can understand, but...

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.080
it's about time to surface, even for just a little bit.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:07.040
You know that you can't stay like that forever.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:20.080
Hey.

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:25.500
I said, hey!

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.500
You can at least answer me, dumbass!

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.500
Don't keep pretending to be asleep!

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:39.080
Do you even get what kind of resolve
Sensei had to have to break up?!

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.790
The reason why Sensei took all the blame
and made a tough decision,

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:46.670
was because she feared that your dream
would be messed up because of her, right?!

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.960
If you're gonna be like that...

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.790
then everything Sensei did would have been for nothing!

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:59.080
I understood that... but...

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:02.130
not that I could be so powerless...

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:06.000
To not be able to do anything. And in this way...

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.960
Hina... Hina...!

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:15.830
Speaking of, your hair stinks. At least take a bath.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.380
I'm sorry to bother you during break.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:34.500
I was hoping that you'd let me take a break
from submitting my weekly short stories for a while...

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:37.290
That is all up to you.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:41.250
Instead of that, please let me write
a somewhat longer one.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:46.420
If I don't write that... then I can't move on.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.630
...during spare moments

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.630
here and there, we...

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.080
Natsuo...

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.170
How is Natsuo-kun doing?

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.080
No change; he's still holed up.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.080
I see...

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:16.920
On my way home from work, I stopped by
that investigative firm that I'd asked help from,

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.880
and they found out where Hina is.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:19.670
Really?

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:20.710
Yes.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:24.290
It appears that she rented a place near her new post.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.880
I'm just glad for now that I found out she's safe...

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:28.420
Yeah...

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:32.580
We shouldn't tell the kids about this...
Especially Natsuo-kun...

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:33.420
You're right.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:39.580
But, to be honest, I still don't believe it.
That Natsuo and Hina-san were...

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.750
The two of us...

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:46.290
Should we not have gotten remarried after all?

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.670
Want to have some cocoa?

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.000
I put a little ginger in it, so it should warm you up.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.040
Sure...

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.250
So, the gates to the Heavenly
Rock Cave remain shut, huh...?

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:18.880
But instead of sleeping all day like he was,
he's begun to write a novel, right? That's a step forward.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:23.170
But, it's kinda like he's driving himself
into a corner, and...

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:25.000
it looks like he's gonna wreck his health...

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:29.250
Yeah, that one seriously loses all focus on everything
else, once he gets totally absorbed in something.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:33.670
Hey, Rui-Rui.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.550
The Forest Bath

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.550
Sauna

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.550
Medicinal bath

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.550
Microbubble bath

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.550
Body massage

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.670
Natsuo-chan!

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:41.540
Hey...

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.420
I'm glad you came!

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:47.580
You did say, "if you don't come,
I'll sling you over my shoulders and kidnap you."

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.880
Huh? Natsuo-chan, you didn't know?

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.960
You didn't hear about it from Rui-Rui?

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.540
No, nothing...

00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:59.630
By the way...

00:11:59.790 --> 00:12:02.000
Why a public bathhouse...?

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:05.580
I thought that it'd be good for you,
if you took a nice long bath, felt refreshed,

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:08.540
and cleared up your head.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:18.040
You see, my family's been
in the yakuza business for generations.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:22.040
When I cut ties with my parents and left the "family,"
my old man was fired up with anger.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:26.630
While he was flying into a rage, he was crying.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:30.630
After I left home, I was free.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:35.040
There was no need for me to hide the real me.
I could also go out with the person I loved.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:38.960
About the time that I was thinking
of getting rid of this thing on my back...

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:42.170
I received word that my old man had died.

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:49.250
Apparently, it was end-stage cancer. A rather
uncomplicated end for a Yakuza boss, you know?

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:53.330
When I recall how my old man looked that last time...

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:57.790
and when I thought about how he must've felt,
I couldn't even go to his funeral.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.330
Natsuo-chan.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:06.790
As long as you're alive, a lot of things can happen in life.
You can't turn back time, and you can't undo things.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:12.790
All you can do, is shoulder it all
as a part of yourself, and keep on living.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.380
I made a late-night snack, if you want it.

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:24.080
It's good.

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:26.460
Thanks.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.460
Sure...

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:46.090
...in a reproachful tone...

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.260
...in a reproachful tone...

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.720
...oneself...

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:55.170
...the water...

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:55.170
...a veil...

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:55.140
...lashed out...

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:57.380
The sound of the  
rain hitting echoed...

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:57.380
As I passed the usual
row of ginkgo trees...

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.130
To worry about pointless things...

00:13:57.380 --> 00:13:59.130
A drop ran down that face... like a veil.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.630
The window of a parked car...

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.630
The more we stayed together the
more I hid, even my real intentions

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.630
...enveloping...

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.860
The rainbow bridge...

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.860
...the rain...    

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.860
Even still...

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.860
The rainbow-like

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.860
arrangement of words...

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.860
I received from you...

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:13.880
Is there any sign that he'll come down yet?

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:15.170
No.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:16.330
I see...

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.500
But...

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:20.630
He's probably... okay.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.920
The End

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:43.210
Morning. You're up early.

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.460
I thought I'd make ozoni.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:52.670
I see. I lost track of the days. I just found
out that today is New Year's from the TV.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.080
Did you... finish?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:02.420
I drew upon everything that I've got right now,
threw it at it, and poured into it...

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.830
I kinda feel like I've turned into a hollow shell.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:11.330
I don't know if it'll be interesting,
but if you don't mind, will you read it, too?

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:12.920
Sure...!

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.210
Natsuo...!

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:19.330
I am sorry for making you worry.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.630
Are you... okay now...?

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:26.750
Yeah. I realized that I couldn't just stay like that...

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.630
I see... I see...!

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:32.290
It's unfortunate that Hina-san isn't here, but...

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:35.290
let's have a proper New Year's,
so that it'll be a good start to the year!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.420
Wow! It's a sea of people...

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.540
Rui-Rui, Natsuo-kun!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.750
Everyone...?

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.130
I contacted them.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.380
Nat-chan, I see you got through it!

00:15:54.380 --> 00:15:55.170
Huh?!

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:58.960
Sorry. I was exchanging texts
with everyone in the Literature Club.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:03.830
But since this was your problem to work out on your own,
Fujii-kun, we decided to quietly support you.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:06.750
I see. You guys were all there for me, too...

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:08.380
Nat-chan, what's that in your hand?

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:12.330
Oh yeah. I thought I'd have Kiriya-sensei
take a look at my finished draft, so...

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.380
Then, let's all go to Kiriya-sensei's house!

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:16.170
What?!

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.170
Myu-chan, you wanna go too, right?

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:19.710
Oh! Uh...!

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:22.830
Happy New Year!

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:26.330
Mr. Kiriya, you live in an amazing place!

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:26.960
Hey!

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.170
Pardon our intrusion...

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.750
Sensei, here's a little gift of amazake!

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:31.630
Just what is going on here...?

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:32.960
I'm sorry.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.630
My draft's finished and...

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:37.830
Was it necessary to come on New Year's Day?

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:50.670
Note: A famous quote attributed
to the painter, Pablo Picasso.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:50.630
"Art is born of sadness and suffering."

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.580
And yet, I never thought he'd transform this much.

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:25.920
Would you mind keeping next Sunday open?

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:29.500
I wonder why Sensei would ask me
to come over to his house...

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:31.710
Welcome.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.830
My apologies. I know it's your day off.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:34.580
It's fine...

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.580
There's someone I just wanted you to meet.

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.750
So, you're Natsuo Fujii-kun!

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.920
Well, hello!

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:45.750
Uh, h-hello.

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.210
How do you do?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.330
Nice to meet you.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:50.880
U-um... And this person is...?

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:56.630
Sorry for the late introduction. My name
is Soichiro Tsutaya. I came to kidnap you today.

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.330
Huh?!

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.330
Grand Prize Ceremony

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.330
77th Shinkosha

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.330
Literary Art

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.080
Nice dumbfounded look!

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:11.880
Huh...? Shinkosha, as in like "Bungeikato" and stuff...?

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:16.210
Yes. Amongst literary awards,
one could say it's probably the most famous.

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:17.540
Why are we here...?

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:23.170
Actually, I had secretly submitted the novel that you
showed me on New Year's, for these awards.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:24.500
See? Over there.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.870
Amateur Division

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.870
First Prize

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.870
"Well,

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.870
See You."

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.870
Natsuo Fujii

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:31.790
Awesome reaction!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.460
Come on, the order of
the Amateur Division speeches start early.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.960
S-speech...?!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:37.830
Please hurry towards the front.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:48.250
Um... This feels like an incredible honor and...
I don't know what to say...

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:52.830
I was able to finish writing this novel
not just by my own efforts,

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:56.080
but by the support of the people
who are important to me.

00:18:56.290 --> 00:19:00.130
To be honest, I'm not sure
that I can write a story like this ever again,

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:03.040
and it might just be a fluke that I received an award, but...

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:08.000
for the people who supported me as well, I will
do my best to aim for my dream to become a novelist!

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.710
Shinkosha Literary Art Awards

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.710
Amateur Division

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.710
First Prize

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.710
"Well, See You."

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.710
Natsuo Fujii

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:18.960
That was a good speech. However...

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:25.710
Winning that award was not a fluke.
Without a doubt, your heart is what created that work.

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:31.210
Also, although this is a belated formal introduction,

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:35.170
Tsutaya-san here is an editorial staff member
of Shinkosha's Literary Department.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:37.250
Once again, I look forward to working with you.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.210
Tsutaya-san will be the person
in charge of you from now on.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.250
I'm hom-

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:48.290
Hina...

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.170
Hina!

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.040
Hina...!

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:59.540
I wanted to see you... I really wanted to see you...

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.210
There's so much that I want to tell you...!

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:05.710
Hina, there's something today you'll be surprised-

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.100
Natsuo Fujii

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.100
"Well, See You."

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.100
First Prize

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.100
Amateur Division

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.100
Shinkosha LiteraryArt Awards

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.880
Rui, is it okay if I come in?

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.630
Why did you do that?

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:33.710
When I said "I want to grow out my hair,"
Momo lent it to me.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:41.920
The novel I wrote during winter break
won first prize in Shinkosha's Literary Art Awards.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:46.290
Honestly, I still can't believe it, but...

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:49.250
Congratulations.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.330
It came with prize money, too.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:54.040
Can you believe it's 300,000 yen? Isn't that amazing?

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.000
I know, I'll get you something too-

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:00.330
Earlier, when you mistook me
for Hina-nee and hugged me...

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:02.460
You were about to cry, weren't you?

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:05.210
Well, you were crying in your room, too.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.670
I mean, I did suddenly scare you and all.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:09.710
That's not it.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:15.630
Tightly... To be held so tightly...

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:21.420
When I realized that intensity was the epitome
of your feelings for Hina-nee, I started crying.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:29.670
Also, when I thought, "Oh, so this must be
how Hina-nee felt like, always being held"...

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:31.830
I kinda...

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:34.420
What's with you?

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:38.170
Did you do it with Hina-nee?

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:41.670
Huh?! What's up with that?!
Are you crazy?! Why would I tell you...?

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:42.750
Did you?

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:49.630
W-we did... I mean, we were going out, so...

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:54.500
Huh...?! What the...?!

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:58.580
I didn't think much of it
when you and I did it for the first time...

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:01.630
But now... would it be different...?

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:07.580
I...

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:11.040
won't hold back for Hina-nee anymore.

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:19.790
Ah kimi ni dake wagamama ni natte yuku
Ah, I'll be selfish to you

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:24.750
Domestic Girlfriend

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:32.420
Sasai na hibi no nandemo nai yasashisa wo
Your little kindness in normal days

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:42.000
Daiji ni shimatte nandomo akete nagamete iru
I cherish them and open them often to look

00:22:42.580 --> 00:22:50.880
Kimi no honshin kikezu ni karamawari shitari shite
I wouldn't be able to ask you about your feelings and losing my self

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:49.130
Sensei, goodbye!

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:50.290
Goodbye!

00:22:51.040 --> 00:22:59.170
Kantan na koto hodo muzukashiku natte iru
The easiest things become harder to do

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:03.130
Otona ni nareba
If I become an adult,

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:03.460
About Sensei's hair. Don't you think its kind of a waste?

00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:07.790
Yeah? I like it better now, it gives a neat impression.

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:15.580
Konna koto de nayamazu ni umaku ikirareru kana
I can live well without worrying about something like this?

00:23:16.460 --> 00:23:20.880
Ah kimi ni dake wagamama ni naru
Ah, I become selfish just towards you

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:25.080
Dondon jibun rashiku mo nakunatte
I'll lose my self more & more

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:29.630
Ah mata kimochi ga sakibashitte
Ah, my feelings get ahead of myself again

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:30.550
Bungikato

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:30.550
77th Literary Artists Awards

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:30.550
Amateur Division

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:30.550
First Prize

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:30.550
"Well, See You."

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:30.550
Natsuo Fujii

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:34.130
Dondon matomo ja nakunatteku kara
I can't stand it more

00:23:34.130 --> 00:23:39.580
Sotchi wo minai de
Don't look that way
